<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Exp Med</journal-id><journal-title>The Journal of Experimental Medicine</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0022-1007</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-9538</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">19870040</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2132148</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>THE RELATION OF HEART WEIGHT TO THE BASAL METABOLISM AS VARIED BY THYROID ADMINISTRATION</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>Francis M.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>MacKay</surname><given-names>Eaton M.</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="N0x3ab5e30N0x38325a8">From The Scripps Metabolic Clinic, La Jolla, California</aff><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>31</day><month>5</month><year>1932</year></pub-date><volume>55</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>903</fpage><lpage>909</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>6</day><month>3</month><year>1932</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; Copyright, 1932, by The Rockefeller Institute for Medical Research New York</copyright-statement></permissions><abstract><p> A linear relationship exists in the albino rat between the heart weight and the basal metabolic rate when varied by the administration of active thyroid material. It is suggested that this increase in heart weight which follows the increase in metabolism after thyroid is in the nature of a simple work hypertrophy of the myocardium. </p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>